        {
          "id": 698520720,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The backticks \"`\" work great for HTML (grey shading) but nothing is added for the text version:  \n```\nYou can use Help › About Wireshark › Folders or tshark -G folders to find the default locations\n  on your system.\n```\nDo anyone read the release notes and are they more likely to check the html or text version?  \n  \n\nThe menu macro works in HTML and txt file. Does not work in Gitlab. ([AsciiDoc menu levels are not sufficiently visually separated](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/issues/325943))  \nWho is target for [docbook/README.adoc](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/docbook/README.adoc) and where (what tool) will they read it in? Should `docbook/README.adoc` be fudged to display properly in Gitlab with the actual macros left in the file as comments when someone reads the source file?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
